# Files where one unreviewed change does the most damage. A pull request that touches any
# of them asks their owner for a review. Add a file here when it runs beside the update
# signing key, decides what the app's page may do, or reaches users without a release.

# Workflows, the build action and release scripts: the signed builds run them beside the
# update signing key. This file too, so no one can take themselves off it unseen.
/.github/                             @Mateusz-Jaskolowski

# What every build runs: npm scripts and Vite's config run in the signed builds too.
/package.json                         @Mateusz-Jaskolowski
/vite.config.ts                       @Mateusz-Jaskolowski

# The shell's security settings: the Content Security Policy, the updater's public key
# and address, and which shell commands the page may call.
/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json            @Mateusz-Jaskolowski
/src-tauri/tauri.unsigned.conf.json   @Mateusz-Jaskolowski
/src-tauri/capabilities/              @Mateusz-Jaskolowski
# The browser version's headers: its Content Security Policy is what keeps its page from
# sending anything anywhere else.
/public-web/                          @Mateusz-Jaskolowski

# Live without a release: the Workers behind updates.strandivo.com, which every installed
# copy asks, and feedback.strandivo.com (with the rules it bundles), and the website, which goes live on every push to main, with what it is
# written from (its generator, its pages' sources and the privacy page).
/services/updates/                    @Mateusz-Jaskolowski
/services/feedback/                   @Mateusz-Jaskolowski
/src/lib/feedback.ts                  @Mateusz-Jaskolowski
/site/                                @Mateusz-Jaskolowski
/tools/build-site.mjs                 @Mateusz-Jaskolowski
/tools/site/                          @Mateusz-Jaskolowski
/docs/privacy.md                      @Mateusz-Jaskolowski

# Where security problems are reported.
/SECURITY.md                          @Mateusz-Jaskolowski
